questions.question:
Consider the following code snippet:

x = 15
if x < 10:
    print('Less than 10')
elif x < 20:
    print('Less than 20')
else:
    print('20 or more')

What will be printed when the code is executed?

What is the output of the following code snippet?

x = 5
if x > 3:
    if x > 4:
        print('A')
    else:
        print('B')
else:
    print('C')
